# Markdown Tables

Use **minimal** separator rows. Do not pad `---` dashes to match column width.

```markdown
<!-- ❌ BAD — padded separators -->
| Module | Symbol | Evidence | Recommendation |
|--------|--------|----------|----------------|
| `foo.js` | `bar` | Tests only | Remove |

<!-- ✅ GOOD — three dashes per column is enough -->
| Module | Symbol | Evidence | Recommendation |
|---|---|---|---|
| `foo.js` | `bar` | Tests only | Remove |
```

Rules:

- Separator cells: `---` only (or `:---` / `---:` / `:---:` for alignment)
- Never stretch dashes to align with the longest cell in each column
- Column content width does not need to match header or separator width
